}

% CAVEAT for the disp_rate gradient: across species, dispersal distance
% scales with plant height more than seed mass, so tall woody perennials
% often disperse farther than annuals. The short-dispersal perennials in
% this model are meant to represent herbaceous / bunchgrass perennials,
% whose clumping comes largely from clonal (vegetative) spread. The high
% disp_rate at low z is a stand-in for that, not a claim about seed
% dispersal distance per se.
@article{thomson2011dispersal,
